       C99, POSIX.1‐2001.

       The variant returning _d_o_u_b_l_e also conforms to SVr4, 4.3BSD, C89.

       SUSv2 and POSIX.1‐2001 contain text about overflow (which might set
       _e_r_r_n_o to EERRAANNGGEE, or raise an FFEE__OOVVEERRFFLLOOWW exception).  In practice, the
       result cannot overflow on any current machine, so this error‐handling
       stuff was just nonsense.  (More precisely, overflow can happen only
       when the maximum value of the exponent is smaller than the number of
       mantissa bits.  For the IEEE‐754 standard 32‐bit and 64‐bit floating‐
       point numbers the maximum value of the exponent is 127 (respectively,
       1023), and the number of mantissa bits including the implicit bit is 24
       (respectively, 53).)  This was removed in POSIX.1‐2008.

